    Let $(u_n)_n$ a sequence in $S$ such that
    $$
        \lim_{n->oo}\int_0^T\Eb|u_n(t)-u(t)|^2dt = 0.
    $$
    Then one can take a subsequence while using same notation such that
    $$
        \lim_{n->oo}\Eb|u_n(t) - u(t)|^2 = 0\quad "(a.e.)"\ t\in[0,T].
    $$
    Fix any such $t$. Since the projection $f |-> \Eb[f|\Wc_t]$ is continuous in
    $L_2$, we have $\Eb[u_n(t)|\Wc_t] -> \Eb[u(t)|\Wc_t]$ as $n->oo$.
